        "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "Contiguous input-order adjacency lists and one-time ID resolution should reduce scattered linear scans and repeated tokenization. Sequential neighbor passes and cached iterative path evaluation may also improve locality and avoid recomputing shared paths. The baseline is only about 12 ms, so the speed benefit is an unmeasured hypothesis.",
