        "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "A flat row-major byte matrix should reduce allocation and bit-proxy overhead in repeated permutation checks. Comparing sorted row sums first should also reject some non-isomorphic graph pairs before exhaustive search, while retaining the exact search whenever the necessary invariant matches.",
        "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
          "files": [
