      {
        "id": "77770fa58d824433",
        "role": "B",
        "parent_id": null,
        "delegation_parent": "R/B",
        "integration_sources": [],
        "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "A stamped occupancy map built once per expanded state should replace repeated serial box scans in each candidate move, while sorted insertion with memmove should replace quadratic bubble sorting. This removes avoidable loop dependencies without changing the canonical box key or BFS behavior.",
        "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
          "files": [
            "src/sokoban.c"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Build a generation-stamped box occupancy/index map once for each expanded state and use constant-time occupancy checks for the four candidate moves.",
            "Maintain canonical sorted box positions by removing and reinserting the moved box with shifts and binary search instead of bubble-sorting the full array.",
            "Reject moves and pushes that leave board bounds before accessing board cells."
          ]
        },
        "status": "valid",
        "mean_seconds": 0.004763748186330001,
        "commit": "7ebe5c5ce95233e6dd0d00f0b17ff0a1080f4f60"
      },
      {
        "id": "46ab767aae144de8",
        "role": "C",
        "parent_id": null,
        "delegation_parent": "R/C",
        "integration_sources": [],
        "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "On broad Sokoban BFS frontiers, successor legality checks and coordinate sorting are independent across states. Static OpenMP work sharing in bounded 64-state batches may reduce this transition cost on the four-core target, while serial insertion in the original BFS and move order preserves deterministic solution selection. Smaller batches remain serial to avoid parallel overhead.",
        "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
          "files": [
            "src/sokoban.c"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Extract successor-coordinate generation into a side-effect-free helper that can process states concurrently.",
            "Work-share full 64-state frontier batches with OpenMP static scheduling; process smaller batches serially.",
            "Commit generated successors serially in the existing parent and direction order to preserve BFS behavior and tie selection."
          ]
        },
        "status": "valid",
        "mean_seconds": 0.004877431318163872,
        "commit": "32385136c25afba62eee04bc806127cf31ea40d5"
      },
      {
        "id": "a100ba049a9f4c5f",
        "role": "A",
        "parent_id": null,
        "delegation_parent": "R/A",
        "integration_sources": [],
        "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "The box-position vector is stored contiguously and can be kept sorted, so binary searches can replace repeated linear membership scans and a push can restore order by shifting only the affected interval. This may reduce transition work, especially where the existing sort loop runs for every move.",
        "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
          "files": [
            "src/sokoban.c"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Use binary search over the sorted box-position vector to find the adjacent box and detect an occupied push destination.",
            "Replace per-move bubble sorting with a contiguous insertion shift only when a box is pushed; leave the vector untouched for walking moves."
          ]
        },
        "status": "valid",
        "mean_seconds": 0.0049540021767218905,
        "commit": "ea2ce710516488f50891f2fecb7c3011ac1ab05f"
      },
      {
        "id": "0f062ab333a84c7e",
        "role": "B",
        "parent_id": "77770fa58d824433",
        "delegation_parent": "R/B",
        "integration_sources": [],
        "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "Splitting the polynomial hash into independent even-index and odd-index recurrences should shorten the loop-carried dependency chain in state hashing, while combining them with the correct powers of 31 preserves the exact uint32_t hash and BFS state identity.",
        "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
          "files": [
            "src/sokoban.c"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Replace the serial Horner hash loop with two independent stride-two Horner accumulators using 31^2, then combine them with a factor of 31 and process any remaining item. Unsigned 32-bit modular arithmetic preserves the original hash for every box count."
          ]
        },
        "status": "valid",
        "mean_seconds": 0.004805220291018486,
        "commit": "93c54beef5b025e68b0a577e52193191bdcfee57"
      },
