        "integration_sources": [],
        "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "The distance block remains legally SIMD-vectorizable, while top-k insertion is dependency-constrained. When the candidate list contains no NaNs, a candidate at least as far as the current kth distance cannot enter the list, so rejecting it before the serial scan should preserve strict tie ordering while reducing dependent comparisons.",
        "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
