        "role": "B",
        "parent_id": null,
        "delegation_parent": "R/B",
        "integration_sources": [],
        "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "The outer target-body iterations have no loop-carried dependency: each reads positions and writes only its own velocity. A GCC vectorization hint may enable SIMD across targets while leaving each target's sequential j accumulation order intact.",
        "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
          "files": [
            "src/nbody.c"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Added a GCC ivdep hint to the outer body_force loop so the compiler can vectorize independent target-body iterations without asserting independence for the reduction over j."
