        "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "Replacing dense companion-matrix exponentiation with compact Kitamasa polynomial exponentiation should reduce work from O(N^3 log H) to O(N^2 log H). Contiguous coefficient vectors and a wide scratch polynomial also improve locality while avoiding modular reduction on every multiply-add.",
        "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
